---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy | Ops Error Atlas"
	description="Read how Ops Error Atlas handles analytics, ad preparation, and limited visitor data."
>
	<section class="page-hero section-inner">
		<h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
		<p class="page-intro">
			This site is built to stay simple. It uses limited analytics and may display advertising
			after approval, but it does not intentionally collect sensitive personal data.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section class="section section-inner">
		<div class="text-panel rich-copy">
			<h2>Analytics</h2>
			<p>
				The site may use lightweight traffic analytics or Google Analytics to understand which
				pages are useful and which search queries bring visitors.
			</p>
			<p>
				Analytics, if enabled, are used to improve technical content and navigation. The site
				does not require user accounts, subscriptions, or profile creation.
			</p>
			<h2>Advertising</h2>
			<p>
				Advertising may be added later through Google AdSense after approval. If advertising is
				enabled, ad providers can use cookies or similar technologies to deliver, personalize,
				and measure ads according to their own policies.
			</p>
			<p>
				During the approval and preparation stage, the site may include publisher verification
				metadata without displaying ad units.
			</p>
			<h2>Personal data</h2>
			<p>
				This site does not require account creation and does not intentionally request
				sensitive personal data. If you send feedback by email, the message content and email
				address are used only to reply.
			</p>
			<h2>Content and external tools</h2>
			<p>
				Command examples and diagnostic guidance are provided for educational and operational
				reference. You should verify commands in your own environment before using them on
				production systems.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
